  "answer_text": "Elena Gilbert turns into a vampire during the transition between the end of Season 3 and the beginning of Season 4 of *The Vampire Diaries*. \n\nHere is the breakdown of how and when it happens:\n\n### 1. Her \"Death\" (Season 3, Episode 22: \"The Departed\")\nElena is run off Wickery Bridge by Rebekah Mikaelson while in a car with Matt Donovan. When Stefan Salvatore arrives to rescue them from the underwater wreck, Elena selflessly insists that he save Matt first. Because of this, Elena drowns. \n\nUnbeknownst to Stefan, Elena had been treated earlier that day by Dr. Meredith Fell for a severe brain hemorrhage. To save her life, Dr. Fell had secretly administered Damon Salvatore's vampire blood. Because she died with vampire blood in her system, Elena wakes up on a slab in the morgue at the very end of the episode.\n\n### 2. The Transition (Season 4, Episode 1: \"Growing Pains\")\nThough Elena's heart stopped in the Season 3 finale, she is not yet a fully functioning vampire; she is in \"transition.\" In the Season 4 premiere, she has 24 hours to feed on human blood or she will die permanently. \n\nElena initially resists, as she never wanted to become a vampire. However, after being captured by the Founder's Council alongside Stefan and Rebekah, she begins dying from starvation. Stefan manages to overpower a guard to get his blood to Elena, allowing her to feed and officially complete her transition into a vampire.",
